{"id":"osmosis-diffusion","title":"Biology: osmosis and diffusion","subject":"Biology","label":"JAMB · WAEC","exams":["jamb","waec"],"language":"en","seconds":184,"duration":183.61,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":482,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":14.565},{"id":"explain","title":"Diffusion","start":14.565,"end":46.185},{"id":"explain2","title":"Osmosis","start":46.185,"end":90.825},{"id":"example","title":"Cucumber example","start":90.825,"end":117.405},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":117.405,"end":128.345},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":128.345,"end":139.405},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":139.405,"end":160.215},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":160.215,"end":183.61}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":6,"text":"You sprinkle salt on cucumber slices for a salad, and in a few minutes they go soft and watery.","w":[0.52,0.7,1.12,1.46,1.62,2.14,2.58,2.76,2.84,3.66,3.8,3.9,3.98,4.18,4.5,4.66,4.9,5.4,5.54]},{"s":0,"a":6.3,"b":10.36,"text":"Nobody squeezed them. So where did the water come from, and what pulled it out?","w":[6.42,6.88,7.24,8.06,8.2,8.4,8.52,8.64,8.94,9.14,9.48,9.6,9.8,10.02,10.18]},{"s":0,"a":10.81,"b":14.14,"text":"I'm Kora, and by the end of this you'll answer that yourself.","w":[10.9,11.08,11.92,12.06,12.22,12.44,12.6,12.7,12.94,13.26,13.54,13.7]},{"s":1,"a":14.99,"b":16.15,"text":"Start with diffusion.","w":[15.08,15.38,15.56]},{"s":1,"a":16.45,"b":24.67,"text":"Diffusion is the net movement of molecules or ions from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration, down a concentration gradient.","w":[16.46,17.06,17.16,17.3,17.54,17.88,18.02,18.64,18.9,19.3,19.48,19.58,19.88,19.98,20.3,21,21.16,21.26,21.58,21.72,22,23.24,23.48,23.56,24.2]},{"s":1,"a":24.97,"b":29.71,"text":"That means from crowded to less crowded. It continues until they're evenly spread.","w":[25,25.22,25.52,25.8,26.38,26.58,26.82,27.76,27.86,28.46,28.7,28.98,29.36]},{"s":1,"a":30.01,"b":33.02,"text":"No energy from the cell is needed, so it's passive.","w":[30.12,30.42,30.78,30.94,31.08,31.34,31.46,32.24,32.42,32.6]},{"s":1,"a":33.32,"b":36.31,"text":"Picture the smell of frying stew drifting across the room.","w":[33.32,33.7,33.88,34.22,34.38,34.8,35.18,35.58,35.94,36.06]},{"s":1,"a":36.61,"b":39.33,"text":"Or oxygen moving from your air sacs into your blood.","w":[36.66,36.92,37.36,37.66,37.82,38.06,38.24,38.68,38.9,39.06]},{"s":1,"a":39.63,"b":45.76,"text":"Things that speed it up: a steeper gradient, higher temperature, smaller molecules, and a larger surface area.","w":[39.64,39.92,40.12,40.38,40.52,41.06,41.2,41.6,42.28,42.6,43.42,43.84,44.5,44.62,44.72,45.12,45.48]},{"s":2,"a":46.61,"b":47.65,"text":"Now osmosis.","w":[46.68,47.06]},{"s":2,"a":47.95,"b":55.37,"text":"Osmosis is the movement of water molecules from a dilute solution, which has higher water potential, to a concentrated solution.","w":[48.04,48.7,48.82,48.96,49.44,49.58,49.9,50.5,50.68,50.76,51.12,52.04,52.22,52.44,52.8,53.1,53.96,54.12,54.22,54.9]},{"s":2,"a":55.67,"b":58.75,"text":"That concentrated solution has lower water potential.","w":[55.74,56.04,56.76,57.32,57.58,57.94,58.26]},{"s":2,"a":59.05,"b":65.13,"text":"It passes through a selectively permeable membrane. That membrane lets some particles through and blocks others.","w":[59.14,59.28,59.76,60,60.1,60.82,61.38,62.34,62.6,63.02,63.22,63.4,63.84,64.2,64.34,64.72]},{"s":2,"a":65.43,"b":71.76,"text":"So osmosis is water only, and it always needs a membrane. It's passive too, no energy.","w":[65.54,65.88,66.6,66.74,67.16,67.94,68.06,68.24,68.58,68.82,68.88,69.72,69.88,70.28,71.14,71.38]},{"s":2,"a":72.06,"b":77.1,"text":"In pure water a plant cell becomes turgid, and the cell wall stops it bursting.","w":[72.12,72.28,72.6,73.12,73.22,73.56,73.8,74.22,75.16,75.28,75.48,75.8,76.2,76.56,76.66]},{"s":2,"a":77.4,"b":81.08,"text":"In strong salt solution it goes flaccid, then plasmolysed.","w":[77.46,77.62,78.04,78.32,78.9,79,79.28,80.06,80.28]},{"s":2,"a":81.38,"b":87.52,"text":"A red blood cell has no wall, so in pure water it swells and bursts, called haemolysis.","w":[81.48,81.6,81.84,82.16,82.46,82.7,82.88,83.64,83.84,84,84.3,84.72,84.88,85.42,85.56,86.38,86.7]},{"s":2,"a":87.82,"b":90.4,"text":"In strong salt it shrinks, called crenation.","w":[87.86,88.04,88.48,88.88,89.02,89.58,89.88]},{"s":3,"a":91.25,"b":92.23,"text":"Here's the cucumber.","w":[91.28,91.56,91.66]},{"s":3,"a":92.53,"b":96.54,"text":"Ada slices a cucumber, or a garden egg, and sprinkles salt on it.","w":[92.62,92.88,93.34,93.4,94.26,94.42,94.5,94.94,95.24,95.38,95.86,96.2,96.34]},{"s":3,"a":96.84,"b":101.61,"text":"The salt dissolves on the surface, so that surface layer becomes a concentrated solution.","w":[96.84,97,97.32,97.86,97.96,98.08,98.86,99,99.26,99.68,99.98,100.36,100.44,101.1]},{"s":3,"a":101.91,"b":105.22,"text":"The cells inside are more dilute, with higher water potential.","w":[101.92,102.1,102.42,102.8,102.92,103.12,103.86,104.06,104.42,104.72]},{"s":3,"a":105.52,"b":109.78,"text":"Water moves out of the cells, through their membranes, into the salty layer.","w":[105.56,105.92,106.36,106.5,106.6,106.74,107.42,107.66,107.84,108.7,108.92,109.06,109.44]},{"s":3,"a":110.08,"b":112.8,"text":"So the slices soften and water collects in the bowl.","w":[110.14,110.3,110.42,110.84,111.42,111.58,111.9,112.3,112.38,112.48]},{"s":3,"a":113.1,"b":116.98,"text":"That's osmosis at work, not the salt pulling the water out by force.","w":[113.12,113.38,113.94,114.04,114.68,114.86,115.02,115.36,115.68,115.78,116.14,116.32,116.5]},{"s":4,"a":117.83,"b":118.51,"text":"Quick check.","w":[117.88,118.14]},{"s":4,"a":118.81,"b":122.55,"text":"A red blood cell and a plant cell are both placed in distilled water.","w":[118.88,118.98,119.22,119.54,119.96,120.08,120.16,120.5,120.88,121.04,121.34,121.7,121.8,122.24]},{"s":4,"a":122.85,"b":125.27,"text":"What happens to each one, and why?","w":[122.92,123.16,123.56,123.74,124.08,124.7,124.88]},{"s":4,"a":125.72,"b":127.92,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[125.76,126.1,126.4,126.54,126.82,127.42,127.58]},{"s":5,"a":128.77,"b":133.6,"text":"The red blood cell swells and bursts, because water enters and it has no cell wall.","w":[128.77,128.9,129.12,129.42,129.74,130.18,130.3,131.2,131.5,131.9,132.36,132.48,132.56,132.82,133.04,133.28]},{"s":5,"a":133.9,"b":138.98,"text":"The plant cell becomes turgid but does not burst, because the cell wall resists the pressure.","w":[133.92,134.08,134.42,134.7,135.12,135.66,135.82,136.04,136.28,136.96,137.26,137.42,137.7,138,138.48,138.6]},{"s":6,"a":139.83,"b":141.04,"text":"Three mistakes to avoid.","w":[139.86,140.1,140.54,140.7]},{"s":6,"a":141.34,"b":145.68,"text":"One, never say water moves from high concentration to low concentration.","w":[141.52,142.22,142.5,142.72,143.06,143.38,143.6,143.84,144.6,144.76,144.98]},{"s":6,"a":145.98,"b":149.29,"text":"Say high water potential to low water potential instead.","w":[146.08,146.34,146.56,147,147.56,147.74,147.98,148.32,148.82]},{"s":6,"a":149.59,"b":155.04,"text":"Two, don't forget the membrane. Osmosis needs a selectively permeable membrane.","w":[149.62,150.36,150.62,150.94,151.06,152.2,152.84,153.12,153.22,153.96,154.56]},{"s":6,"a":155.34,"b":159.79,"text":"Three, plant cells don't burst in pure water. The wall holds them.","w":[155.38,156.14,156.48,156.84,157.12,157.44,157.56,157.88,158.68,158.82,159.2,159.5]},{"s":7,"a":160.64,"b":161.24,"text":"Recap.","w":[160.76]},{"s":7,"a":161.54,"b":164.98,"text":"Diffusion moves any molecules down a concentration gradient.","w":[161.54,162.12,162.52,162.72,163.34,163.58,163.68,164.44]},{"s":7,"a":165.28,"b":169.84,"text":"Osmosis moves only water, through a membrane, from higher to lower water potential.","w":[165.38,165.94,166.28,166.54,166.94,167.18,167.24,168.06,168.28,168.62,168.76,169.06,169.36]},{"s":7,"a":170.14,"b":171.24,"text":"Both are passive.","w":[170.24,170.52,170.66]},{"s":7,"a":171.54,"b":176.66,"text":"Exam tip: if a question mentions a membrane and water, write osmosis.","w":[171.62,172.1,172.82,172.96,173.04,173.54,173.96,174.06,174.56,174.7,175.62,176]},{"s":7,"a":176.96,"b":180.27,"text":"If it mentions a gas or a smell spreading, write diffusion.","w":[177.04,177.14,177.26,177.66,177.76,178.22,178.34,178.44,178.74,179.46,179.72]},{"s":7,"a":180.57,"b":183.01,"text":"Well done. Keep learning with Knowzone.","w":[180.74,181.02,181.7,181.98,182.28,182.46]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Cucumber puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Salt on cucumber → soft, watery"},{"at":6.2,"kind":"text","text":"Where does the water come from?"},{"at":10.71,"kind":"text","text":"Goal: explain it yourself"}]},{"at":14.74,"heading":"Diffusion","items":[{"at":16.35,"kind":"term","text":"Diffusion","detail":"Net movement of molecules/ions: high → low concentration"},{"at":24.87,"kind":"text","text":"Crowded → less crowded; until evenly spread"},{"at":29.91,"kind":"text","text":"Passive: no energy from cell needed"},{"at":36.51,"kind":"text","text":"Examples: stew smell; O₂ air sacs → blood"},{"at":39.53,"kind":"text","text":"Faster: steeper gradient, heat, small molecules, large SA"}]},{"at":46.36,"heading":"Osmosis","items":[{"at":47.85,"kind":"term","text":"Osmosis","detail":"Water from dilute (higher water potential) to concentrated solution"},{"at":55.57,"kind":"text","text":"Concentrated solution = lower water potential"},{"at":55.57,"kind":"clip","text":"Water crosses the membrane; the bigger solute cannot (AI animation)","src":"clip.mp4"},{"at":58.95,"kind":"term","text":"Selectively permeable","detail":"Membrane: lets some particles through, blocks others"},{"at":65.33,"kind":"text","text":"Osmosis: water only; needs membrane; passive"}]},{"at":71.81,"heading":"Cells in solutions","items":[{"at":71.96,"kind":"text","text":"Plant cell in pure water → turgid; wall prevents burst"},{"at":77.3,"kind":"text","text":"Strong salt → flaccid, then plasmolysed"},{"at":77.3,"kind":"image","text":"Plasmolysed plant cells in salt solution (microscope)","src":"plasmolysis.webp","credit":"Mnolf · CC BY-SA 3.0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":81.28,"kind":"term","text":"Haemolysis","detail":"Red blood cell swells and bursts in pure water"},{"at":87.72,"kind":"term","text":"Crenation","detail":"Red blood cell shrinks in strong salt solution"}]},{"at":91,"heading":"Salt on slices","items":[{"at":92.43,"kind":"text","text":"Ada salts cucumber or garden egg slices"},{"at":101.81,"kind":"text","text":"Surface concentrated; cells dilute (higher water potential)"},{"at":105.42,"kind":"text","text":"Water leaves cells → salty surface layer"},{"at":109.98,"kind":"text","text":"Slices soften; water collects in bowl"},{"at":113,"kind":"text","text":"Osmosis, not salt pulling water by force"}]},{"at":117.41,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":117.41,"kind":"question","text":"A red blood cell and a plant cell are both placed in distilled water. What happens to each one, and why?"}]},{"at":128.52,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":128.67,"kind":"text","text":"Red blood cell swells, bursts: water enters; no wall"},{"at":133.8,"kind":"text","text":"Plant cell turgid, not burst: wall resists pressure"}]},{"at":139.58,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":145.88,"kind":"wrong","text":"Water: high concentration → low concentration"},{"at":149.49,"kind":"wrong","text":"Osmosis needs no membrane"},{"at":155.24,"kind":"wrong","text":"Plant cells burst in pure water"}]},{"at":160.39,"heading":"Recap and tip","items":[{"at":161.44,"kind":"text","text":"Diffusion: any molecules down concentration gradient"},{"at":165.18,"kind":"text","text":"Osmosis: water only, membrane, high → low water potential"},{"at":170.04,"kind":"text","text":"Both passive (no cell energy)"},{"at":171.44,"kind":"tip","text":"Membrane + water in question → write osmosis"},{"at":176.86,"kind":"tip","text":"Gas or smell spreading → write diffusion"}]}],"check":{"at":128.17,"seconds":10,"question":"A red blood cell and a plant cell are both placed in distilled water. What happens to each one, and why?","answer":"Red blood cell swells and bursts (no cell wall); plant cell becomes turgid but does not burst (wall resists pressure)."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"Rhoeo Discolor - Plasmolysis.jpg","author":"Mnolf","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhoeo_Discolor_-_Plasmolysis.jpg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}